.KEY args/F
; OpenCMR2 for WarpOS on the Radeon 9200 MiniGL R200 stack.
; Run from the game drawer:  Execute OpenCMR2-WOS [args]
; (Not "OpenCMR2": AmigaDOS names ignore case, and that is the executable.)
; The drawer holds opencmr2, minigl_ppc.dll and minigl_ppc_host next to the
; game data. Boot protocol: cold boot, then this script.
; Quit a remote session with:  SetEnv OPENCMR2_QUIT 1
FailAt 21
Delete ENV:OPENCMR2_QUIT QUIET
; The R200 stack's settings for this minigl_ppc.dll. CP emit must stay on
; (performance, and presents fail without it). A tiled render target
; (MINIGL_CTILE) and a left-over engine lease are removed: with them
; presents failed and the host stopped. CP present stays off: with it the
; picture had wrong colours and diagonal bands.
; The compact vertex formats (MGLPPC_TCL6, MGLPPC_TCL5) are for 2D clients:
; with both set the stage's distant scenery was drawn smeared. TCL6 alone
; saves under a millisecond a frame and is not proven safe, so it stays off.
Delete ENV:MGLPPC_LEASE ENV:MINIGL_CTILE QUIET
Delete ENV:MGLPPC_TCL6 ENV:MGLPPC_TCL5 QUIET
SetEnv MGLPPC_CPEMIT 1
SetEnv MGLPPC_CPPRESENT 0
SetEnv MGLPPC_HOSTPRI -1
SetEnv MGLPPC_NOALTIVEC 1
; minigl_ppc.dll starts minigl_ppc_host from PROGDIR: itself; a second host
; started here would conflict with it.
Stack 1048576
opencmr2 <args>
